A||||5||Shiner||Has Anybody Shipped A Nose Before?||||1||
Z||000000||Shiner||11-08-2000||01:24 AM||||Has anybody done this?  It seems to be over the size that UPS, FedEX, and the "oversize package" from the US Postal Service, will do.  I was just wondering HOW you would go about shipping this, and what it will cost? Zip code 54455 to 18077.<BR> <BR>TIA!<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-08-2000||02:13 AM||||Shiner, contact a common carrier - a truck lines  -- they can give you the rate and ship it for you....... that's the way we ship large pieces.......<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||11-08-2000||02:24 AM||||If paint condition isn't an issue then you can fold the ends over and tape them down.  It will then fit into a box small enough to meet UPS standards.  <P>It's been awhile since I have shipped a fascia, but last time it was about $20.  I hear that UPS has changed the way they rate oversized boxes, so it may be more $$.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-08-2000||03:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>If paint condition isn't an issue then you can fold the ends over and tape them down.  It will then fit into a box small enough to meet UPS standards</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You're joking, right?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-08-2000||04:15 AM||||Not at all.  I have shipped many fascias (front and rear) this way.  It will crack the paint, but if paint condition doesn't matter to the buyer then no problem.  <P>You would be amazed at how small I can get a fascia!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||ur2biteme||11-08-2000||05:59 AM||||i'm appologizing in advance for this, i'm in a wierd mood tonight:<P>shipping a nose?  i didnt know you could ship body parts, although i know you can get kidneys on e-bay sometimes......  :P||||reg||1
